Looking at the requirements, I need to implement a minimal `mkdir` that:
1. Creates directories (single level, no `-p`)
2. Handles `--` terminator, bare `-` as operand, unknown options as errors
3. Continues after per-operand errors, exits 0 only if all succeed
4. Produces GNU 9.11-style diagnostics to stderr
5. Works with arbitrary byte strings (not just UTF-8)

